  "notes": "### Which file do I need?\n\n| You have | Download |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Windows** | `..._x64-setup.exe` |\n| **Mac, Apple Silicon** (M1-M4) | `..._aarch64.dmg` |\n| **Mac, Intel** | `..._x64.dmg` |\n\nWindows also has an `.msi` if your workplace prefers one. The\n`.app.tar.gz`, `.sig` and `latest.json` files are used by the\napp to update itself - you do not need to download them.\n\nOn a Mac, Homebrew picks the right build for you:\n\n```bash\nbrew tap Carkappa/snaptrack https://github.com/Carkappa/Snaptrack\nbrew install --cask job-tracker\n```\n\nInstalled copies pick this up automatically.\n\nThe build is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen and macOS\nGatekeeper warn on a fresh install - see the README.",
